        "urlName": "astrild-2"
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "58c62efae9868f3662e9d9a1",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2026-06-03T11:20:28.713Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "deletedAt": null,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "6a13d3e7b94d2b86707854be",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 1
      },
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Being able to turn them off should be a safety setting option. \n\nNot just for those like myself who just find them obnoxious and childish most of the time. Not just for those with low end pcs or standalone headsets who start to lag due to them. But for first and foremost for those with medical conditions. \n\nThey shouldn't be forced to go through a whole instance list to manually turn off everyone's items manually. Let alone they have to keep track of new people joining the instance and turning them off too. I can't imagine how anxious these people must be, despite them trying their best and taking their own responsibility to turn off the items manually. \n\nYou seem to have the technology for it because instance owners can turn them off. Let us do it on a personal base as well.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-05-25T04:45:27.392Z",
  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "There is currently no option to disable fancy portals.\n\nThere is currently no option to disable join/leave animations.\n\nThere is currently no option to disable items without being world host.\n\nHaving an option in safety settings would mitigate performance dips and be safer for users by giving users control of/ the ability to disable uncontrollable particles/ animations. For epileptic and photosensitive users, disabling items individually is tedious and problematic, some of us can not look at items to disable them without risking medical problems. The same can be said for fancy portals and join/ leave animations if people join/leave near you, we do not have control over placement. \n\nGive us an option to disable these in the safety settings.",
